    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **55 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `AssignCustomerCode.java`, the OfficeFloor function step that computes the owner's customer code during the `POST /api/owners` pipeline.\n\n**The change:** The step already computed the base code `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`. I injected `OwnerRepository` (by type, per the function-injection convention) and added a collision check:\n\n- Collect all existing owners' customer codes via `ownerRepository.findAll()`.\n- If the computed base code doesn't collide, use it unchanged.\n- If it does, append `'-<n>'` with the smallest `n` starting at 2 that produces a code not already in use, and return that de-duplicated code.\n\nThis step runs after `BuildOwner` and before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't yet in `findAll()` and never collides with itself. Because later steps (`AssignMembershipNumber`, the Luhn check digit, the audit record, the derived locality) all read the stored `customerCode`, they automatically reflect the de-duplicated value. I also updated the class Javadoc to document the rule.\n\nAll existing customerCode-dependent tests (Cp09/14/16/21/31/32) and the new collision test (Cp41) pass, along with the entire suite.",
